1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you!

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, it's so elusive?

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,837
Even though it's blinding me!

11
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:55,657
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you!

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,597
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see!

15
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,860
Believe in what I do!

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us!

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,557
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,637
We don't want to live ordinary lives.

24
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:39,697
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:42,520
We live in one another.

26
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:54,600
Move it! Get out of our way! Step aside!

27
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:56,100
Hey, isn't that...

28
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:05,440
No, Chaka, please wait!

29
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:09,960
So who are they?

30
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:11,300
The Guardians.

31
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,340
The Kicking Claw Force.

32
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:24,700
Don't attack, men.

33
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:27,693
You'll only be throwing your lives away.

34
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:34,440
They broke the door down. Adari, move.

35
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:37,360
Please, save His Majesty
and Princess Phoebe.

36
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:42,017
Your Majesty, defending you to
the death is not only our mission.

37
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:43,977
It is the highest honor and privilege.

38
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:46,236
Therefore, we can't simply avoid him.

39
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:49,220
He is one of the seven
warlords of the sea.

40
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:52,049
The only way to beat
him is to fight dirty.

41
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:54,420
We four are as one.

42
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:56,520
We fight for your honor.

43
00:02:56,860 --> 00:02:58,220
To set things right.

44
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:02,040
It seems that you have
quite the reputation.

45
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:05,440
Therefore, I will spare your lives.

46
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:06,874
Leave now and go home.

47
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:08,220
We can't do that.

48
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:12,067
There is another reason
we will not withdraw.

49
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:13,770
Reason?

50
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:19,257
If the rumors are true and
you really are the ringleader,

51
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:21,693
the architect of this whole rebellion...

52
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:26,720
Those bruises.

53
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:30,400
What have you men done?

54
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:35,860
Shall I?

55
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:38,707
You needn't waste your
time on these cretins.

56
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:42,840
They didn't.

57
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:48,520
Chaka, what's happening to their bodies?

58
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:52,140
I fear to temporarily
increase their power.

59
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:55,360
They drank the fatal elixir.

60
00:03:55,600 --> 00:04:00,637
It grants incredible strength,
but then kills the host.

61
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:02,960
They're dead men. Oh no!

62
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:08,920
You bulked up to challenge
me, I'm flattered.

63
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:12,672
But what good is victory if
you're not around to enjoy it?

64
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:14,680
Chaka, please,

65
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:17,437
forgive us for doing this
without consulting you,

66
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:22,340
but we had to take drastic measures
to end this country's suffering.

67
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:45,437
those idiots how could they we

68
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:49,040
have to make him realize the fury of

69
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:55,410
This country!

70
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:13,460
That wasn't the smartest decision.

71
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:17,000
A person should value
his life above all else.

72
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:19,940
But it's too late for regrets, yes?

73
00:05:25,460 --> 00:05:30,057
And if you're all going to die anyway, I
don't have to bother killing you myself,

74
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:30,970
right?

75
00:05:31,053 --> 00:05:33,140
You don't even have the decency to fight!

76
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:51,620
Chaka, I'm sorry.

77
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:01,080
Behold the very definition of stupidity.

78
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:03,940
You bastard!

79
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:13,470
Chaka!

80
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:16,060
Chaka, this is senseless.

81
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:18,837
You'll just be following
them to their deaths.

82
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,100
Ah, they're a zone type.

83
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:38,340
I see you share the same flaws
these fools you'll die for others

84
00:06:52,860 --> 00:06:53,720
Damn it.

85
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:55,513
Lost too much, Willett.

86
00:06:57,300 --> 00:07:02,160
Yes, I should be thankful the cuts aren't
that deep, but it does hurt like ow.

87
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,762
Wonder how the others are doing.

88
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:09,337
Want to know what's going on.

89
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:11,040
Idiots better not be dead.

90
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:12,890
What?

91
00:07:12,973 --> 00:07:15,347
What do you mean I have
to pair with eyelash?

92
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:20,740
Look, he's a camel!

93
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:24,318
I'm very fragile so I need
someone who can back me up

94
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:26,520
Man up the raffle was fair.

95
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:30,577
You got eyelash and that's that fine But
you better promise me one thing when me

96
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:32,097
and this stupid camel are standing at the

97
00:07:32,180 --> 00:07:35,160
doorway of death Please
come to our rescue. Sorry.

98
00:07:35,380 --> 00:07:36,860
I only save the damsels.

99
00:07:37,020 --> 00:07:38,079
You're on your own

100
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:47,400
Hey, what's wrong? Usopp?

101
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:49,020
Why are you crying?

102
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:57,777
Yeah, you're crying, yeah, he who
smelt the dilded, yeah, that's it,

103
00:07:57,860 --> 00:07:58,690
you dilded, you dilded,

104
00:07:58,773 --> 00:08:04,260
you dilded, you dilded, you're a dilded, a
dilded smelter, that old hag said, Luffy,

105
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:06,900
she said Luffy's dead,

106
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:10,960
so I, I wonder if it's true, come on,

107
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:14,097
you guys really believe that,
of course not, Luffy's alive,

108
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:15,497
what do you think we are, stupid,

109
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:18,477
that's right, I don't believe
it either, Luffy is alive,

110
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:21,437
yeah, all right, I get it, you're
preaching to the choir here?

111
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:23,917
What we have to do now is
get to the palace ASAP!

112
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,217
Now if you don't mind,

113
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:29,717
try to plug your snot at least until
the rumbling from the battle stops!

114
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:32,577
Don't swallow it!

115
00:08:32,660 --> 00:08:37,617
Thank you everyone!

116
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:39,157
You're welcome!

117
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,577
But it's too early to thank us!

118
00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:41,490
He's right!

119
00:08:41,573 --> 00:08:44,617
Besides, if you really
want to thank pirates you?

120
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:46,177
They have to let us see some goods.

121
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:50,077
Nami, what is it you're trying to
leech out of this country anyway?

122
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:51,340
Is Nami okay?

123
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:54,040
Did she manage to get away?

124
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:02,720
They finally came off.

125
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:07,845
Calling it a powerful one-shot attack, I
think that's a bit of an understatement.

126
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:10,400
The fighting's come far.

127
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:13,168
They're right there,
just around the corner.

128
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:18,940
Guess the situation's changed.

129
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,419
Anyway, I better get to the palace.

130
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:28,241
Sounds like the battle's started.

131
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:29,940
What about Vivi?

132
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,240
Oh, yeah. One more thing.

133
00:09:33,420 --> 00:09:35,891
And this is an important fact to remember.

134
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:39,221
After a battle, these guys
put down a ton of food.

135
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:40,790
Okay.

136
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:43,220
We'll be waiting for you!

137
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:49,340
This is absolutely crucial.

138
00:09:51,620 --> 00:09:53,140
Don't screw this up!

139
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:54,540
Let's go!

140
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:56,380
See you at the palace!

141
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:09,650
Chaka!

142
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:19,540
Weakness is a crime, punishable by death.

143
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:24,240
Phoebe!

144
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:43,540
No, Koza.

145
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:50,417
Koza.

146
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:51,540
It's you.

147
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:55,374
Oh, I see you came through
the shortcut you used to use.

148
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:57,160
This can't be.

149
00:10:57,340 --> 00:10:58,634
What am I seeing here?

150
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:12,860
I came in hope of persuading
the royal army, but...

151
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:22,757
Chaka, and the king is about to
be killed by this country's hero.

152
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:24,580
I can't believe my eyes.

153
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:30,117
Now things are starting
to get interesting.

154
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:32,537
Here we are in the midst of an epic war,

155
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:35,157
and yet the leaders of both
sides aren't on the battlefield.

156
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:37,557
Fate has placed them
squabbling at my feet.

157
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:40,277
A battle to the death
between two broken titans

158
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:43,066
bleeding out the last
remnants of their power.

159
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:48,020
You seem lost and confused.

160
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:50,137
Don't worry, it's a natural reaction.

161
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:51,240
Let me help you.

162
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:57,621
Relax and open your mind, then imagine being
faced with the worst possible scenario.

163
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:04,820
Koza, purge your heart of all suspicion!

164
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:13,840
Do you love this country?

165
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:24,917
This is my home.

166
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,080
Mine as well.

167
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:30,877
Koza, listen.

168
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:35,560
Vivi, who was responsible for the
drought ravaging this country? Tell me?

169
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:40,080
It was that honor belongs to me!

170
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:43,697
Over the past two years
each and every malicious

171
00:12:43,780 --> 00:12:46,839
deed you attributed to the
king's doing was in fact?

172
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:51,897
Perpetrated by my company a trap that
saw you playing right into our hands.

173
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:54,797
It was a flawless systematic
plot of deception.

174
00:12:54,880 --> 00:12:58,597
I Must say it was entertaining
watching as the royal

175
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:02,260
family and its mighty army
desperately chased our shadows

176
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:07,810
Pity.

177
00:13:07,893 --> 00:13:12,468
You probably would have died in ignorant
bliss not knowing these brutal facts.

178
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:19,840
Koza, listen!

179
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:22,730
Majesty.

180
00:13:23,220 --> 00:13:25,817
There's still some time
if you have the courage.

181
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:27,320
You must act now.

182
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:29,481
Save as many citizens as you can.

183
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:35,920
In less than half an hour, the whole palace
square will be blown to kingdom come.

184
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:37,420
What do you mean?

185
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:39,860
So you're still alive, are you?

186
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:46,250
Hurry!

187
00:13:59,180 --> 00:14:00,010
Stop!

188
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:03,510
Vivi!

189
00:14:04,180 --> 00:14:05,160
Get off of me!

190
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:06,170
What are you doing?

191
00:14:06,253 --> 00:14:07,083
There's no time!

192
00:14:07,166 --> 00:14:08,717
The battle is about to
spill into the square.

193
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:11,180
If it's really set to blow up, get off!

194
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:13,640
You have to listen to me!

195
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:18,440
Think this through, please!

196
00:14:18,880 --> 00:14:22,197
What will happen if you tell the
armies the square is set to explode?

197
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:23,398
The men will panic!

198
00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:25,657
It would only add more
chaos to the battle,

199
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:29,152
and even if you stop the bomb,
it won't stop the fighting!

200
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:32,740
Either way, people are still going to die!

201
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,254
You won't save anyone!

202
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:39,250
Understand?

203
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:41,250
Huh.

204
00:14:41,333 --> 00:14:43,480
Well, well, what a perceptive girl.

205
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:48,144
Our only hope is to do what should
have been done from the start.

206
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:53,058
We have to stop the rebellion
and end this bloodshed!

207
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:55,440
And you...

208
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:58,440
You're the only one who can do it!

209
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:20,337
Did you really think I
was going to sit back and

210
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:23,302
watch passively while you
tried to ruin my plans?

211
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:35,390
Chaka!

212
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:41,780
I am Alabaster's guardian deity.

213
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:44,520
I am the Jackal.

214
00:15:47,140 --> 00:15:50,740
I'll fight as long as there
is breath left in my body.

215
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:53,920
Some call that brave, I call it stupid.

216
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:56,277
Do what you must, both of you.

217
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:59,340
I will hold him back
for a few more minutes.

218
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:07,280
Chaka, such a shame the leader
of the Sansan clan is so weak.

219
00:16:12,060 --> 00:16:13,520
Boy, what's the matter?

220
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:22,797
What's wrong with you?

221
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:23,710
I'm a child.

222
00:16:23,793 --> 00:16:24,817
You can't treat me like this.

223
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:26,860
You're a pain in the neck, kid.

224
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:32,200
Koza, you asked me to train you,
or have you forgotten that already?

225
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:48,917
Report from Guard Unit 2 to Headquarters!

226
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,059
Report from Unit 2 to Headquarters!

227
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:53,540
Line four has been breached!

228
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:55,280
Enemy has broken through!

229
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:57,777
The rebel army is
currently passing through

230
00:16:57,860 --> 00:17:00,057
the central plaza heading
to the north block!

231
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:01,728
They will reach the palace!

232
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:04,280
Raise the flag to surrender!

233
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:08,120
Royal army, you will
surrender immediately!

234
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:12,220
Princess of Evie, is she serious? But why?

235
00:17:12,580 --> 00:17:13,540
That's absurd.

236
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:17,387
If we do as she says, that would
mean the end of this country.

237
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:18,760
Hey, look! That's...

238
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:21,260
It's Koza!

239
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:24,437
What is the rebel army's leader
doing here in the palace?

240
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:26,940
Hear me, the princess speaks the truth!

241
00:17:27,340 --> 00:17:31,020
We no longer desire victory,
only to end this conflict!

242
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:33,820
Both sides have spilled enough blood!

243
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:43,420
I will make each and every rebel understand
the pointlessness of this civil war!

244
00:17:44,040 --> 00:17:48,060
They will see, as I do, that we
no longer have reason to fight!

245
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:51,837
In the interest of restoring
peace and preserving life,

246
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:54,840
I ask you, wave the white flag! Please!

247
00:17:56,220 --> 00:17:58,640
The king's head will roll this day!

248
00:17:59,300 --> 00:18:02,140
Oh, I can see the clock tower up ahead!

249
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:10,640
We're approaching the palace square!

250
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:13,240
Prepare to attack!

251
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:24,800
Wait! Stop!

252
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:34,120
White flags?

253
00:18:34,420 --> 00:18:36,940
The royal army is waving white flags!

254
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:38,440
We did it!

255
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:39,542
They surrender!

256
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:44,740
It's Koza!

257
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:47,360
The battle is over!

258
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:52,935
Sir, everyone, quiet your
anger and lower your weapons.

259
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:55,600
The royal army will stand down.

260
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:57,918
Let no more blood stain the streets.

261
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:02,900
Please, listen to him.

262
00:19:19,380 --> 00:19:21,180
Is this the truth, Koza?

263
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:22,790
Yes.

264
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:24,549
The battle's finally over.

265
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:43,560
Cousin!

266
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:47,260
Cousin!

267
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:52,390
Cousin!

268
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:55,920
You just wait until it's finished.

269
00:19:56,260 --> 00:19:59,980
This town will bring good fortune
and joy to so many people.

270
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:02,277
It's going to be the best town ever.

271
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:06,242
When it's up and running, I'll
personally give you the grand tour.

272
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:14,780
Don't fight Rebel Army.

273
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:19,100
Don't fight them.

274
00:20:25,980 --> 00:20:29,100
How can they shoot Koza? Get them!

275
00:20:35,300 --> 00:20:36,800
It's the rough works!

276
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:46,760
What did you do?

277
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:47,959
Why did you shoot?

278
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:58,020
Listen to me now, Rebel Army.

279
00:20:58,320 --> 00:20:59,900
Do not fight.

280
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:04,297
What's going on?

281
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:06,262
Where'd the sandstorm come from?

282
00:21:06,980 --> 00:21:08,440
Listen, Rebel Army.

283
00:21:13,020 --> 00:21:14,620
They're shooting at us.

284
00:21:14,780 --> 00:21:15,760
How dare they?

285
00:21:24,140 --> 00:21:26,787
Where did all the sand
come from so suddenly?

286
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:28,214
We can't see anything.

287
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:35,480
Damn it! Bastards!

288
00:21:40,940 --> 00:21:42,437
Don't shoot carelessly!

289
00:21:42,520 --> 00:21:43,540
What's going on?

290
00:21:44,020 --> 00:21:46,314
They still don't know what's happening.

291
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:47,577
What's going on, you idiots,

292
00:21:47,660 --> 00:21:51,954
is that Baroque Works members are
posing as soldiers in both your armies.

293
00:21:57,020 --> 00:21:57,960
Stop now!

294
00:21:58,420 --> 00:22:00,300
Come on, just hang in there!

295
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:09,780
They aren't surrendering.

296
00:22:10,760 --> 00:22:14,289
Thought they'd ambush us by
raising a phony white flag, huh?

297
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:17,280
So this is how the
Royal Army plans to win.

298
00:22:17,860 --> 00:22:19,920
By using dirty tricks like that!

299
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:26,740
Stop it!

300
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,360
No, don't do this!

301
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:30,080
Please, stop fighting!

302
00:22:30,500 --> 00:22:31,340
Soldiers!

303
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:32,800
Look up here!

304
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:38,300
Stop, Rebel Army.

305
00:22:38,740 --> 00:22:40,080
Stop this.

306
00:22:40,340 --> 00:22:41,840
This battle is...

307
00:22:56,060 --> 00:22:58,420
Hey, are you okay? Damn.

308
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:01,700
Now, Royal Army, launch counter-attack!

309
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,177
Stop it!

310
00:23:35,260 --> 00:23:36,480
Stop fighting!

311
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:40,720
Please don't fight.

312
00:23:42,620 --> 00:23:43,840
Stop now!

313
00:23:44,500 --> 00:23:47,500
You fought long and hard,
princess, and did well.

314
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:50,357
But now...

315
00:23:50,440 --> 00:23:51,420
Give up.

316
00:23:52,140 --> 00:23:56,700
Your voice will no longer
reach them so this is it.

317
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:06,940
You have to run away vv get away
from him before it's too late!

318
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:16,000
I won't.

319
00:24:21,360 --> 00:24:23,000
You made this dust, devil.

320
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:25,009
It's your doing, isn't it?

321
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:30,840
But still, there's time.

322
00:24:31,860 --> 00:24:34,837
If I stop the explosion that's
scheduled in 15 minutes,

323
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:37,508
I can still reduce the
number of casualties.

324
00:24:42,220 --> 00:24:44,637
If I try this, the rebellion will stop.

325
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:47,420
If I try that, the rebellion will stop.

326
00:24:48,540 --> 00:24:50,364
It's time to wake up, princess.

327
00:24:51,840 --> 00:24:54,300
I'm tired of your useless idealism.

328
00:24:54,460 --> 00:24:55,695
It's gotten pathetic.

329
00:24:58,820 --> 00:25:03,037
What good are your happy ideals if you
can't do anything to make them reality?

330
00:25:03,120 --> 00:25:05,002
Then they're nothing but dreams.

331
00:25:05,540 --> 00:25:08,040
And your dreams don't stand a chance.

332
00:25:11,180 --> 00:25:13,592
I don't care what you think of my ideals.

333
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:16,779
I'm never going to give up on them!

334
00:25:20,280 --> 00:25:21,980
You would never understand!

335
00:25:22,680 --> 00:25:25,327
I'm this country's
princess, I won't give up!

336
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:27,420
I won't give in no matter what!

337
00:25:32,780 --> 00:25:34,960
You really are a sad little girl.

338
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:38,000
I refuse...

339
00:25:39,180 --> 00:25:40,280
to give up!

340
00:25:43,140 --> 00:25:46,180
I will save Alamaster!

341
00:25:48,120 --> 00:25:48,980
Alamaster!

342
00:25:53,600 --> 00:25:54,460
VV!

343
00:25:58,820 --> 00:26:02,600
You have only fifteen minutes
until the square is blown up.

344
00:26:03,880 --> 00:26:07,920
More of the rebel forces are
gathering as reinforcements arrive.

345
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:14,900
One after another, without even realizing
they're marching to their death.

346
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:29,717
You know, you could have let the Royal Army
know about the coming explosion earlier.

347
00:26:29,800 --> 00:26:32,257
If so, maybe there
would have been a panic.

348
00:26:32,340 --> 00:26:36,222
But then you could have saved tens
of thousands of innocent lives.

349
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:38,580
Stop it!

350
00:26:39,020 --> 00:26:40,160
Please, crocodile!

351
00:26:40,620 --> 00:26:41,780
Just let her go!

352
00:26:45,860 --> 00:26:50,389
In the end, your plans for saving this
country have done more harm than good.

353
00:26:50,800 --> 00:26:53,597
Your wretched failures
have only ended up hurting

354
00:26:53,680 --> 00:26:56,860
the precious citizens
who you love so dearly.

355
00:27:02,420 --> 00:27:04,920
From the beginning of my operations here,

356
00:27:05,060 --> 00:27:08,001
the sheer stupidity of
your country has amused me.

357
00:27:09,780 --> 00:27:12,240
So pathetic, so easy to manipulate!

358
00:27:18,980 --> 00:27:23,540
You did a decent job of spying on
our company for the past two years,

359
00:27:23,800 --> 00:27:25,480
I will grant you that much?

360
00:27:26,560 --> 00:27:28,060
It's me, Vivi.

361
00:27:28,320 --> 00:27:29,800
Don't you recognize me?

362
00:27:31,380 --> 00:27:32,697
I look different.

363
00:27:32,780 --> 00:27:34,840
I lost some weight, I suppose.

364
00:27:36,160 --> 00:27:40,807
But when it was all said and done, you
really had no hope of changing anything.

365
00:27:41,860 --> 00:27:43,213
Stopping the rebellion.

366
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:44,700
Saving the kingdom.

367
00:27:45,580 --> 00:27:49,060
All those worthless ideas
you've clung to for so long.

368
00:27:49,600 --> 00:27:53,260
In the end, they just
created more victims for me.

369
00:27:54,800 --> 00:27:56,700
Let me tell you something.

370
00:27:58,460 --> 00:28:00,813
You're never going to save this country!

371
00:28:03,800 --> 00:28:05,000
Goodbye, princess.

372
00:28:31,940 --> 00:28:34,960
Ah ha ha ha ha...

373
00:28:49,940 --> 00:28:51,420
It can't be.

374
00:28:53,580 --> 00:28:54,980
Crocodile!

375
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:01,680
Luffy!

376
00:29:04,040 --> 00:29:06,280
It can't be!
